s3.amazonaws.com%2F0c%2Fed%2F531138be47c49ce4464c171a3451%2Flynch-ange-smith-install.jpg","line":74,"embedded":true},{"title":"Sight and Sound","target":"https://www.bfi.org.uk/sight-and-sound/news/sight-sound-september-2024-issue","line":84}],"metadata":{"title":"White picket fences and pipe bombs: How David Lynch’s Boise childhood inspired uncanny filmmaking","source":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/news/2025-01-24/human-ear-idaho-david-lynch-death-blue-velvet-boise","author":["[[Julie Luchetta]]"],"published":"2025-01-25","created":"2026-07-20","description":"David Lynch, the director of cult classics such as Twin Peaks, Mulholland Drive and Eraserhead passed away last week. Known for his cryptic storytelling, surrealist imagery, and eerie moodiness, the filmmaker’s career was defined by a distinct visual style, perhaps shaped by his childhood in suburban Idaho.","tags":["#idaho"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},